Alembic migrations.

Run from the `backend/` directory:

    alembic upgrade head          # apply
    alembic downgrade -1          # roll back one revision
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"

The database URL comes from DATABASE_URL via env.py -- it is not stored in
alembic.ini, so no credentials are committed.

Always read an autogenerated revision before applying it. Alembic cannot infer
intent: a renamed column looks identical to a drop plus an add, and applying that
blindly deletes data.
